WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.080
A planet 1000 light years away has vanished from view because a neighbor tilts its orbit like a top. This is Fascinating Frontiers, episode 249. Twin spacecraft have finished Earth flybyes on the way to Mars. Mid-infrared data have pinned down a comet nucleus, and a rare stellar pair has been caught mid-interaction.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:27.840
T-O-I 2535-B, Fizz.org reports, is a hot Jupiter on an 8.25-day orbit, and tests watching

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.420
the system between 2019 and 2026 recorded transit times shifting by up to 6 hours.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.280
An unseen neighbor's gravity sets both planets wobbling, swinging each world out of alignment

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.040
with our line of sight, so the transits we used to catch no longer cross the star from

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:50.040
here. Follow-up measurements from the WIAN 3.5 meter telescope confirmed the planet's

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.840
size and temperature, and the next possible transit window sits between 2056 and 2076.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.300
The geometry points to violent formation pathways for some hot Jupiters that leave tilted

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:08.291
orbits rather than flat, co-planar systems, escape aids, twin smallsats, aviation week reports,

00:01:09.071 --> 00:01:13.851
completed powered Earth flybys nearly a year after launch, and the national aeronautics

00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:15.831
and space administration, or NASA,

00:01:16.371 --> 00:01:17.991
pair is now on course for Mars.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.511
The spacecraft left their loiter orbits

00:01:20.511 --> 00:01:23.931
after those flybys and began the interplanetary cruise phase.

00:01:24.491 --> 00:01:26.851
And mission teams confirmed the trajectory adjustments

00:01:26.851 --> 00:01:29.671
place both vehicles on the correct path for arrival.

00:01:30.351 --> 00:01:32.171
Once they get there, the twins will study

00:01:32.171 --> 00:01:34.231
Mars' magnetosphere and atmosphere.

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:37.486
A few kilometers of ice and rock can race

00:01:37.486 --> 00:01:40.526
through the inner solar system at tens of kilometers per second

00:01:40.886 --> 00:01:42.966
and still look from Earth like nothing more

00:01:42.966 --> 00:01:48.626
than a fuzzy point of light. Subaru Telescope mid-infrared instruments, Fizz.org reports,

00:01:49.266 --> 00:01:54.746
turned on Comet 2P Enki, and found a nucleus that is not a sphere but an elongated body

00:01:54.746 --> 00:02:00.026
about 7 kilometers along the long axis, and about 3 kilometers along the short axis.

00:02:00.646 --> 00:02:06.006
That outline is comparable to a small city pulled into a rough oval, turning once every

00:02:06.006 --> 00:02:11.066
few hours and showing different faces to the sun. Mid-infrared wavelengths read temperature

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:16.286
directly, so as the nucleus spins, the surface warms and cools, and the changing brightness

00:02:16.286 --> 00:02:21.466
traces the projected area and the thermal properties of the body. By modeling how the

00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:26.646
emission varied over a full rotation, the team extracted both axes and found the surface

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:33.046
reached 328 plus or minus 7 Kelvin at the time of observation. That temperature is hot

00:02:33.046 --> 00:02:37.926
enough to drive the comet's activity, and still fits a dark, low albedo surface that

00:02:37.926 --> 00:02:39.426
soaks up sunlight efficiently.

00:02:40.066 --> 00:02:44.706
The same wavelength separate the solid nucleus from the surrounding coma of dust and gas,

00:02:45.306 --> 00:02:50.286
because visible light scatters off the coma and can hide the true size of the body, while

00:02:50.286 --> 00:02:53.606
mid-infrared light comes mostly from the warmer nucleus itself.

00:02:54.266 --> 00:02:58.646
That separation lets astronomers measure the nucleus even when the comet is active

00:02:58.646 --> 00:03:03.406
and optically bright, and these data give the first direct constraints on Enky's shape

00:03:03.406 --> 00:03:05.886
from ground-based mid-infrared observations.

00:03:05.886 --> 00:03:11.486
What is still unknown is how typical that stretched form is among other short period comets.

00:03:11.746 --> 00:03:16.666
Because repeated close passes by the sun could grind nuclei towards spheres or break them

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:17.886
into irregular shards.

00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:21.706
And only a handful of nuclei have been measured at this level of detail.

00:03:22.486 --> 00:03:27.826
An unusual stellar pair shows an odd configuration that astronomers say is rarely caught in progress.

00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:32.126
A snapshot of how stars evolve when they interact closely with a companion.

00:03:32.126 --> 00:03:38.793
While most Milky Way stars are main sequence objects still fusing hydrogen into helium, Jupiter

00:03:38.793 --> 00:03:44.713
and Mars, Space.com reports, will appear strikingly close together in the constellation Leo on

00:03:44.713 --> 00:03:49.073
November 15th, sitting in the same small patch of sky as seen from Earth.

00:03:49.573 --> 00:03:52.513
You can find the parallel in the eastern sky before dawn.

00:03:53.514 --> 00:03:58.834
The Ampere Challenge invites United States companies to develop and demonstrate 3-7 kilowatt

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:05.074
Hall Effect thruster prototypes, with a total prize of $500,000. Up to two teams can

00:04:05.074 --> 00:04:12.454
each win $250,000, plus access to NASA testing facilities. Registration closes January 27th,

00:04:12.454 --> 00:04:18.334
2027, and the program targets capabilities needed for satellite, defense, and exploration missions.

00:04:19.476 --> 00:04:24.476
Perseverance, University Day reports, is carrying fabric swatches for Washington University

00:04:24.476 --> 00:04:29.256
researchers examining how Martian dust interacts with those materials on the rover.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:33.516
The experiment records how particles adhere to and abrade the swatches

00:04:33.516 --> 00:04:37.616
under actual Martian conditions, and the data will help future crews prepare

00:04:37.616 --> 00:04:39.136
for dust storms on the surface.

00:04:40.192 --> 00:04:44.752
A digital composite from Sardinia, NASA reports, shows Saturn disappearing

00:04:44.752 --> 00:04:48.792
behind the moon during an occultation visible from Greenland through Central

00:04:48.792 --> 00:04:51.512
Europe and Northern Africa in early 2025.

00:04:51.512 --> 00:04:51.712
5.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:58.012
The image combines three exposures taken after sunset, with the star 85 Aquaria visible

00:04:58.012 --> 00:05:02.632
near Saturn, and the next such event visible from Earth occurs in 2031.

00:05:03.797 --> 00:05:09.357
Long-lived mineral grains, fizz.org reports, survive impact events, and preserve records

00:05:09.357 --> 00:05:14.097
of shock and heating, retaining signatures that allow scientists to determine when and

00:05:14.097 --> 00:05:15.997
how intensely those collisions occurred.

00:05:16.717 --> 00:05:20.997
Researchers are using them to reconstruct the timing and effects of impacts on Earth,

00:05:20.997 --> 00:05:26.996
the moon and other bodies. Two nearby rocky worlds could let observers on their surfaces

00:05:26.996 --> 00:05:32.396
see neighboring planets appear to move backward across the sky. A geometry that arises from

00:05:32.396 --> 00:05:37.356
the specific orbital alignments in the system and creates a parent retrograde motion for

00:05:37.356 --> 00:05:44.016
anyone standing there. Beijing China Daily Reports reaffirmed its stance on cooperative, non-military

00:05:44.016 --> 00:05:49.256
space activities during recent international discussions, emphasizing multilateral efforts

00:05:49.256 --> 00:05:51.256
over unilateral actions in orbit.

00:05:52.387 --> 00:05:56.867
Chandra X-ray Observatory detected X-ray emission from AT-2016 blue,

00:05:57.307 --> 00:06:00.607
that is at least 100 times brighter than earlier observations,

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:04.567
and the data point to a stellar mass black hole or neutron star

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:08.247
pulling material from the massive star every 113 days.

00:06:08.807 --> 00:06:13.707
The system produced at least 27 optical outbursts between 2012 and 2026.

